{
  "title": "ArcCivs 0.1.89: road material and width, optional board and cosmetic storage",
  "assumptions": [
    "Low/base/high assumptions are 1/4/6 active villages, 0.25/1/4 active hours per village-day and 16/64/256 worked road columns. These are sensitivities, not measured production. A three-wide profile has more eligible columns; it does not multiply the one-column work rate.",
    "Before .89: one changed centerline floor costs 1 abstract STONE and uses cobble or cobble stairs. After: one actually worked column still costs 1 STONE, whether floor replacement or bounded clearance-only work; flats use DIRT_PATH, slopes dry bottom OAK/SPRUCE/DARK_OAK stairs selected by existing style. A column writes at most one floor plus four exact AIR cut cells; cleared natural blocks produce no drops. Existing paid plans and receipts retain their original blocks and amounts.",
    "No healthy-column charge, no additional infrastructure/stock/population cap, no native inventory grant or refund. Next ordinary construction goal retains its stone reserve. Auto abstract stock cannot be withdrawn as items. Existing public approaches can still be mined; no new protection restriction is introduced.",
    "Alternative player interception: mine every new floor, sell exactly its one native drop, and force repeated paid maintenance while surplus stock lasts. Spawn disk read 2026-10-25T21:12:07Z via RCNet 6272101fafd7259fd7d6520386a51aa8fec1a8639cde37c2cfbaccb9ae03568c shows COBBLESTONE SELL 0.05 and DIRT SELL 1 Vault in Blocks.yml SHA 66f548fcc63969a32443e4f9a5e4ab97438d44ac25f623467997a0126946c4e4; all three wooden stairs SELL 0.88 in Crap.yml SHA 41c1df2838f4b912f18319b3c71b90c23ac88bcca6c8d0b49373d4ef11230df8. These are nominal disk prices, not active in-memory quotes or observed sales. DIRT_PATH drops one DIRT without Silk Touch; all-flat dirt is the conservative 1 Vault ceiling. Silk Touch/other items and stairs are alternatives, not additive payouts.",
    "The existing three-second column work gives a loose 1200 columns/hour ceiling before actual walking, sleep, cooldown and finite stock. Thus adversarial all-flat resale changes the nominal ceiling from 60 to 1200 Vault/hour per builder while stock lasts. Existing L1/L2/L3 quarry stone deliveries replenish at most 180/360/540 STONE per worker-hour before travel; conditional resale ceilings become 180/360/540 Vault/hour per quarry worker versus prior 9/18/27. Ore cycles replace stone cycles. Admin stock grants are finite test input, not ordinary sustainable earnings.",
    "The optional automatic PLAN_BOARD reuses its existing price 12 WOOD + 8 STONE, paid once after first house unless already accepted/active; established full sixteen-plot villages skip this new optional goal. No additional job, beds, output, recurring payout or cap change. The calculator founding-day board event occurs once, not every day.",
    "Warehouse alignment changes only chest states: 275 chest blocks and 7425 physical slots before/after across nine templates. Pair repair skips either occupied/viewed/PDC/protected/changed half, keeps contents and requires explicit existing repair. No automatic world migration. Captured construction remains immutable.",
    "Idle handoffs and neutral no-assignment status issue no work cycles, XP, resources or Trails wear. The deterministic runtime check measures walk cadence in a fixture; restored real production after activation is unmeasured.",
    "Fresh Trails disk read 2026-10-25T21:11:42Z SHA 9cfca23bef314cb042bf121947ccf8a61a14aa86c9c98265d68685598713fc64 retains DIRT_PATH 1.3, COBBLESTONE 1.25/1.28, COARSE_DIRT 1.2. Registration uses only the existing surface multiplier, no stacking. Maximum all-travel path ratio is 1.3/1.28=1.015625 or 1.3/1.25=1.04 versus old cobble, 1.3 versus unboosted ground; actual whole-cycle effects depend on travel fraction. Stationary work, sleep and nominal producer output remain unchanged.",
    "Direct Vault, tokens, player XP and resident XP are separately zero. Conditional intercepted-floor sale is the only modeled monetary mint and cannot be added to the same retained world floor. Current EconomyShopGUI SELL stays current; planned SELL-off/contracts is future, with conditional road resale zero only once that transition is actually active.",
    "Decision: accept the requested material/width change with the existing finite stock sink, paid receipts, next-goal reserve and rate. Do not silently add caps or reprice the shop. The increased conditional dirt resale is explicit; live incidence, player sale access and actual throughput remain unknown and must be observed after a separately authorized activation."
  ],
